# Five peers. Radios 3 and 4 also carry an outsider's transmitter: from 2 s each floods the ground station's name, where
# the drones report, with 2 000 junk wires a second, from 17 s with 20 000 (6.4 Mbit/s, an IP mesh radio's rate), until
# 32 s; drone-3 and drone-4 on those radios are honest. Junk wears the version byte its radio last heard, so every wire
# costs gcs a tag check, and nothing else. Every drone reports once a second; gcs counts, each second, the reports that
# landed: four, under every sealer, since the simulator charges no CPU time. Signed, gcs is the hub.
seed 53
peers 5
profile reticulum
2000   flood 3 gcs 2000
2000   flood 4 gcs 2000
17000  flood 3 gcs 20000
17000  flood 4 gcs 20000
32000  flood 3 gcs 0
32000  flood 4 gcs 0
2000   telemetry
3000   telemetry
